# Serialize package fetches (yarn 1 default is 8 in parallel).
#
# strut is a git dependency with a `prepare` script. yarn 1 installs such a
# dependency by cloning it and running a nested `yarn install` inside the
# outer one, and both installs write the same cache. Before fetching a
# package yarn deletes its cache entry without taking a lock, so with a cold
# cache and parallel fetches the two installs collide on packages they share
# (@img/sharp-*, rxjs, ...) and the install dies with "Extracting tar content
# of undefined failed" or EEXIST. Serializing the outer fetch queue means the
# nested install runs while nothing else is being fetched. Costs about a
# minute on a cold install; warm installs are unaffected.
network-concurrency 1
